  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 9 actions (analogway_picturall.js:89-302) and 2 boolean feedbacks (lines 306-364), each in a single object literal registered by updateActions/updateFeedbacks. The two feedbacks also have an upgrade script (CreateConvertToBooleanFeedbackUpgradeScript).",
    "Protocol: Picturall server text commands over a plain TCP socket to port 11000 (hard-coded in connectTcp, analogway_picturall.js:859), a newline is appended to every command. Examples sent: `set cue1 playback cue=<n>`, `set stack<n> control command=1`, `set source<n> control play_state_req=<0|5|6>`.",
    "'layer' and 'source' are layer/source numbers of the Picturall (the module's own preset generation assumes 32 layers; the server configuration can change that number, comment at line 15). The text options have no upper limit in their regex.",
    "Regexes are the runtime values of the source strings. In playback_goto the source string '/^0*[1-9][0-9]*(\\.[0-9]+)?$/' (analogway_picturall.js:134) contains a `\\.` inside a normal string, which is just `.`, so the effective pattern is /^0*[1-9][0-9]*(.[0-9]+)?$/ (the dot matches any character).",
    "Playback numbers are 1-8 (regex /^0*[1-8]$/). Option values of the action textinputs are processed with useVariables; the feedback textinputs have no variable support.",
    "The Toggle Play/Pause value 't' in layer_playback toggles between Pause (5) and Play (0) from the module's tracked source play state (lines 209-219); layer is required but has no default.",
    "Presets and variables (playbackN_cuestack/_cue/_state/_progress, software_version and per-source variables) are not catalogued; the module sets `disableVariableValidation` (line 35) because the per-source variables used in presets (elapsed, countdown, playstate) are not all defined in updateVariables.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.4.3: options do not support expressions."
  ]
